<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taceddin Bey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1387</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taceddin Bey was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> chief who founded the Taceddinid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niksar">Niksar</a> in the Pontic hinterland of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> in the mid-14th century, as Ilkhanid authority faded. He married Eudokia, daughter of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a> emperor Alexios III, linking his house with its Greek neighbour, and was killed fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kadi-burhan-al-din">Kadi Burhan al-Din</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sivas">Sivas</a> in the 1380s.</p></div>
